{"text": "STATE OF MICHIGAN\n\nGRETCHEN WHITMER DEPARTMENT OF HEALTH AND HUMAN SERVICES ROBERT GORDON\nGOVERNOR LANSING DIRECTOR\n\nMEMORANDUM\n\nDATE: January 23, 2021\n\nTO: Robert Ernst, University of Michigan\nDanielle Sheen, University of Michigan\nDyan Jenkins Ali, University of Michigan\nEmily Toth Martin, University of Michigan\n\nFROM: Dr. Joneigh Khaldun,\nChief Medical Executive and Chief Deputy Director\n\ncc: Mark Schlissel, University of Michigan\nPreeti Malani, University of Michigan\nChris Kolb, University of Michigan\nJimena Loveluck, Washtenaw County Health Department\nJuan Marquez, Washtenaw County Health Department\nElizabeth Hertel, Michigan Department of Health and Human Services\nNatasha Bagdasarian, Michigan Department of Health and Human Services\nSarah Lyon-Callo, Michigan Department of Health and Human Services\n\nSUBJECT: SARS-CoV-2 B.1.1.7\n\nStaff from the Washtenaw County Health Department are continuing to monitor the outbreak of\nSAR-CoV-2 B.1.1.7 variant virus infections in the University of Michigan (UM) community. To\ndate, B 1.1.7 variant cases have been confirmed or is suspected in members of multiple UM\nathletic teams. As you know, compared to the wild-type virus, the B.1.1.7 variant is\napproximately 50 percent more transmissible, leading to faster spread of the virus, potentially\nincreased numbers of cases, and additional hospitalizations and deaths. Therefore, continued\nidentification of this variant, particularly in a campus setting, requires additional levels of public\nhealth intervention.\n\nGiven continued transmission of the variant within UM Athletic programs, MDHHS is\nrecommending a very aggressive strategy that exceeds current program efforts that had been\ndesigned around the wild-type virus. The core of this strategy places ALL UM varsity athletic\nprograms in quarantine until further notice and up to 14 days from today\u2019s date. This\nquarantine will include clearly delineated restrictions AND assurance monitoring.\n\n1. Cease athletic events and practices, effective immediately.\na. All team members and associated household members, as well as identified\nclose contacts of cases, must immediately isolate/quarantine, starting from\nthe date of this letter. All athletic teams are to be restricted from any outside\ngatherings or contact with non-team members for the duration of this\n\nquarantine.\n333 SOUTH GRAND AVENUE \u00ab PO BOX 30195 e LANSING, MICHIGAN 48909\nwww.michigan.gov/mdhhs e 517-241-3740",
